---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '../data/site';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Editorial Policy', url: '/editorial-policy/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy & Fact-Checking Standards | DormReady"
  description="DormReady's comprehensive editorial standards: research methodology, product selection rules, affiliate disclosure principles, and correction policy."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <div class="bg-cream-100 border-b border-cream-300 py-8 sm:py-12">
    <div class="container-custom max-w-4xl">
      <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />

      <span class="mt-4 inline-block px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-forest-50 text-forest-800 border border-forest-100">
        Editorial Integrity
      </span>

      <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold font-serif text-navy-900 leading-tight">
        Editorial Policy & Standards
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-4 text-base sm:text-lg text-navy-700 leading-relaxed font-sans">
        Trust is our core asset. This policy outlines how DormReady structures dorm gear advice, audits student discounts, handles future affiliate relationships, and manages corrections.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container-custom max-w-4xl py-10 lg:py-14 space-y-12 text-base leading-relaxed text-navy-800">
    <!-- Section 1: Research Process -->
    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-serif text-navy-900">1. Our Research Process</h2>
      <p>
        Our editorial team analyzes residence hall life through four primary lenses:
      </p>
      <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-navy-700">
        <li><strong>Physical Spatial Constraints:</strong> Double rooms average 130–180 sq ft. Products that create clutter or cannot be folded/stacked are filtered out.</li>
        <li><strong>Institutional Fire & Safety Codes:</strong> We cross-reference typical university residence policies across public, private, and regional colleges to ensure suggested items (e.g. UL-listed surge protectors, auto-shutoff kettles) comply with campus safety standards.</li>
        <li><strong>Academic Durability:</strong> College gear must withstand 9 months of intensive daily use, frequent moves between semesters, and transport in campus laundry facilities.</li>
        <li><strong>Total Cost of Ownership:</strong> We prioritize products that provide lasting utility across multiple academic years rather than single-use novelties.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 2: Fact-Checking Standards -->
    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-serif text-navy-900">2. Fact-Checking & Verification</h2>
      <p>
        We hold every factual assertion on DormReady to strict standards:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-navy-700">
        <li><strong>No Fabricated Ratings or Testimonials:</strong> We never generate artificial star ratings, fake student quotes, or synthetic lab scores.</li>
        <li><strong>Explicit Specification Labels:</strong> All hardware reference baselines or specification targets are clearly labeled to prevent confusion with lab benchmark results.</li>
        <li><strong>Discount Audits:</strong> Student discounts must be audited against official vendor terms (e.g., SheerID, UNiDAYS, Apple Education) with logged check dates and direct links.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 3: Product Selection Principles -->
    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-serif text-navy-900">3. Product Selection Principles</h2>
      <p>
        Our editorial team maintains 100% independence when recommending dorm gear:
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="p-5 bg-white border border-cream-300 rounded-xl space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-navy-900 text-sm">What We Prioritize</h3>
          <ul class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-navy-600 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
            <li>UL/ETL safety certification</li>
            <li>Multi-functional utility</li>
            <li>Washable, durable textiles</li>
            <li>Compact, collapsible form factors</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 bg-white border border-cream-300 rounded-xl space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-navy-900 text-sm">What We Disqualify</h3>
          <ul class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-navy-600 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
            <li>Exposed-coil heating elements</li>
            <li>Unfused multi-plug extension cords</li>
            <li>Bulky non-collapsible furniture</li>
            <li>Single-purpose novelty gadgets</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 4: Affiliate Disclosure Principles -->
    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-serif text-navy-900">4. Affiliate Disclosure Principles</h2>
      <p>
        DormReady is designed to be reader-supported. In the future, when readers purchase products through links on our site, we may earn an affiliate commission from merchant partners.
      </p>
      <div class="p-5 bg-cream-100 border border-cream-300 rounded-xl text-sm space-y-2">
        <p class="font-semibold text-navy-900">Our Commercial Guardrails:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-1 list-disc list-inside text-navy-700 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <li>We never accept paid inclusion, sponsored rankings, or promotional placement fees.</li>
          <li>Commercial partnerships have zero influence on whether an item is recommended or cautioned against.</li>
          <li>All merchant links are clearly distinguished and accompanied by prominent disclosure badges.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 5: Correction & Update Policy -->
    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-serif text-navy-900">5. Correction & Update Policy</h2>
      <p>
        College housing rules, product availability, and student discount terms evolve. We conduct seasonal audits prior to major academic move-in cycles.
      </p>
      <p>
        If an error, expired promotion, or outdated specification is identified, our editorial staff updates the page and records the update in the visible <code>Last updated</code> timestamp.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm">
        To submit a correction or housing policy update, open an issue on our <a href={SITE_CONFIG.githubRepoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline text-forest-800 font-semibold">GitHub Project Repository</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
